WEBVTT

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:03.690
<i>Previously on Phantom in the Twilight.</i>

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:08.830
You're looking good, miss.

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:10.360
You're finally yourself again.

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:13.320
Yeah. Thanks, guys.

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.250
You're up early.

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:16.720
Are you sure you're okay?

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.450
There's a reason I have to get up.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.450
Yeah.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.000
Good morning, everyone.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.830
I'm going to go rescue Shinyao.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:20.040
Huh? What's an exhibit doing out here?

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.310
Help!

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.090
<i>Mr. Haysin.</i>

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.850
<i>Why are you scaring ordinary 
people at the English Museum?</i>

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:50.920
You're the one who suggested we play a game.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:55.650
Or is recruiting reinforcements 
against the rules?

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:01.200
Since you supplied me with 
new weapons, I don't mind.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.050
But what are you going to do with 
all those rare and childish cards?

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:08.700
Do you know what we're playing for?

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.790
In case you forgot,

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.920
it's between my Shinyao and your Ton.

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:18.670
Whoever levels the strongest 
character first wins.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:20.180
Those are the rules.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.260
And winner takes all.

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:25.290
That's right.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:29.060
So don't accidentally kill our prize.

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:33.440
If they could be accidentally destroyed, 
then that's all they're good for.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:36.180
<i>Are you sure, though?</i>

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:40.400
<i>Baileu Ton is fairly strong now.</i>

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.820
<i>If it comes down to a fight, 
I'm several steps ahead of you.</i>

00:03:45.300 --> 00:03:47.160
Don't worry.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.620
My princess has potential.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.020
I see. Then I...

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.250
...should train mine as well.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:05.550
So you're insisting on letting yours grow 
up in the wild before capturing her.

00:04:05.990 --> 00:04:08.670
I'll capture mine first and then nurture her

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:12.730
using cutting-edge science 
within the ultimate cage.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:19.400
It seems Shinyao wants 
to go to the Twilights,

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.040
but I won't let something 
so troublesome happen.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:28.620
<b>Episode 9 
The Pursued and The Protector</b>

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:35.420
Shinyao!

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:39.630
What?

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:41.880
Of course not.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.240
Hey, what kind of café is this?

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:45.130
I'm a customer.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:47.160
Sorry.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.800
We're a little busy right now.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:53.270
I had a feeling you were after 
seeing the guys outside.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.240
What happened?

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:55.920
Well...

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:59.360
We received a message from 
my brother a few moments ago.

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:04.380
The eternal rebel finally felt 
like asking his brother for help.

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:07.160
He said he's on his way here with Shinyao.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:10.850
The friend you've been looking for?

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:12.930
I see. That's good news.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:16.290
Or not.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:20.000
Immediately after that, this happened.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.730
We knew they'd tap our phone lines,

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:28.640
but we weren't expecting them 
to analyze their wolf howls.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:33.740
Midnight Sun's Umbra research has 
made more progress than we realized.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:38.040
In any case, I told him 
not to come right now,

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:40.490
but I'm sure they know that, too.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:41.320
Damn!

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:42.760
What a pain in rear!

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:44.790
Should we go chase them off?

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:47.540
Don't. There's no end to them.

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:50.400
Hello?

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.730
What? Monsters have been 
spotted at the museum?

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.800
Business is terrible today.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.120
Let's close shop.

00:06:06.140 --> 00:06:08.040
Let me ask you again.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:11.280
While patrolling tonight, 
nothing strange happened, right?

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.480
You're right.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:15.270
No, nothing strange.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:18.360
Does Vlad erase all the memories of people

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:21.690
who have seen Umbra in this town?

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:25.450
When Gregory asks.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:27.400
Excuse me.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:33.330
We can't let the evil Umbra ruin 
humanity's impression of all of us.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:36.530
Erasing the witness' memory

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:40.920
doesn't change the fact that some 
horrifying monsters appeared here.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:42.960
Were they really that bad?

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:45.930
Yeah. Some fairly dangerous and tough ones.

00:06:45.930 --> 00:06:47.480
Three of them.

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:50.640
If anything happens, I'll let you know imme—

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.030
What?!

00:06:52.030 --> 00:06:52.590
There's one.

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:54.510
Speak of the devil!

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:08.570
Miss, what is that?

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.030
Now's our chance.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:17.230
Ton!

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.640
Lady Ton!

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.860
Ton got stronger again last night.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.810
Damn, I'm jelly.

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:33.480
<i>Really? I should've stayed to watch.</i>

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:35.510
What? You weren't watching?

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:39.980
I wasn't expecting her to 
appear in the first round.

00:07:40.410 --> 00:07:42.480
I wish I hadn't missed the show.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.070
<i>You're hopeless.</i>

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:47.440
I'll send you the video I recorded.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.510
I appreciate it.

00:07:50.040 --> 00:07:52.190
What a convenient age we live in.

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:13.360
Don't worry.

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:15.770
I won't take another precious life.

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:22.930
Though I have hunted enough Umbra 
to know I can't sleep peacefully,

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:25.770
I don't recall doing anything 
to antagonize my beloved humans!

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:32.110
You work for us.

00:08:32.540 --> 00:08:35.450
Who put you up to this? Haysin?

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:37.990
<i>Sir, you're still alive?</i>

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:39.620
You?!

00:08:39.810 --> 00:08:43.070
<i>You said you didn't want to live in disgrace.</i>

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:45.660
<i>Why don't you just die?</i>

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:48.710
<i>I'll handle the company.</i>

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.050
<i>You can rest in peace.</i>

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.040
Bastard.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:55.470
You bite the hand that feeds you? 
 You have no shame.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:08:59.690
However!

00:09:00.860 --> 00:09:03.730
It is a reality that men 
desire personal success.

00:09:04.260 --> 00:09:07.400
Not even God could blame 
you for your ambition.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:09.980
Hate the Umbra, not your fellow man.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:13.050
I forgive all humans.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:13.940
Therefore...

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:19.640
I'll let you off the hook today.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.130
<i>Well? He's grown, hasn't he?</i>

00:09:31.780 --> 00:09:35.340
I understand very well this jolly 
Umbra hunter's current condition.

00:09:35.710 --> 00:09:38.300
So, when will we see Baileu Ton?

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:41.210
<i>Huh? What are you talking abo—</i>

00:09:41.210 --> 00:09:43.880
<i>Oh, sorry. I sent you the wrong file.</i>

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.950
<i>This is what I wanted to show you.</i>

00:09:45.950 --> 00:09:47.730
<i>See? Ton put on quite the performance.</i>

00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:51.360
<i>She's widened the gap again.</i>

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.530
How are you doing?

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:54.980
Shinyao?

00:09:55.580 --> 00:09:59.970
I catch her every once in a while, 
so I know roughly what she's up to.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:03.160
She's given up on meeting 
up with the Twilights

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.750
and has fled into some 
neighborhood somewhere.

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:09.780
I've put up a net in the area.

00:10:09.780 --> 00:10:12.880
It's only a matter of time 
before I capture her.

00:10:16.630 --> 00:10:18.880
I got information on our enemies.

00:10:19.410 --> 00:10:24.510
That Midnight Sun guy sent a bunch 
of soldiers to Camden Town.

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:25.310
What?

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:26.840
Camden.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:30.660
That means there's something there.

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:31.780
Shinyao.

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:33.480
Yeah. I agree.

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:38.360
But they don't know where she is exactly.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.280
Then I have to find her first.

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:42.540
Calm down.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:45.510
They'll use their numbers to find her.

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:48.030
If we try to do the same, we'll fall behind.

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:50.920
We need a plan.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.550
A plan? Like what?

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:55.920
Let me handle it.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:57.540
Camden, right?

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.130
If Chris is there...

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:00.550
Huh?

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:18.640
I can't believe we had the same idea.

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:21.570
It's like we're close brothers.

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:22.990
What is it?

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:24.420
Nothing.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:27.950
Just remembering an old stupid fight.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:30.870
I don't remember how long ago it was.

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:33.790
It's been a long time since 
Chris and I parted ways.

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:37.430
But I haven't forgotten we fought all night

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:42.450
along the canal in Camden the day
 we arrived in London.

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:46.140
Or the sight we saw after we both collapsed.

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:48.520
Then that howl...

00:11:48.830 --> 00:11:52.440
Yeah. I called him and Shinyao there.

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:53.890
I see.

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:57.670
Not even Midnight Sun can analyze 
the memories of two brothers.

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.150
That's an unusually excellent idea from you.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:02.630
Let's hurry.

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:05.990
If they find them first, 
it'll all be for nothing.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.010
Wait. First,

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:11.180
Magic Mirror is installed 
on your phone, right?

00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:11.710
Huh?

00:12:12.270 --> 00:12:15.240
Could you leave it with Toryu?

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:20.090
The Twilights left the café? All of them?

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:23.050
Are they...

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:25.150
heading towards Camden?

00:12:25.150 --> 00:12:26.280
How do they know that?

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:30.270
Oh, the wolves are signaling each other.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:33.950
Which means if we follow them,

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:38.040
they'll tell us where to find Shinyao.

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:44.390
We're too early.

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:47.500
Don't we need to hide?

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:49.110
We are hiding.

00:12:49.110 --> 00:12:51.580
They say the forest is the best
 place to hide a tree.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:56.420
In neighborhoods like this, we'll be harder 
to spot if we blend into the background.

00:12:57.030 --> 00:12:58.840
That's good.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:02.630
I'm actually kind of having fun right now.

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:06.600
It feels like I'm finally 
getting to see London.

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:12.560
Thanks for bringing me 
to this wonderful place.

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:19.390
I'm pretty familiar with this area, 
but if that's how you feel...

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:25.030
Once this crazy situation ends

00:13:25.030 --> 00:13:27.490
and we can go wherever we want,

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:30.700
want to come back here together again?

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:34.160
Yeah. It's a promise.

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:37.190
Yeah. Let's definitely come back.

00:13:51.170 --> 00:13:52.870
They stopped.

00:13:52.870 --> 00:13:55.270
Which means she's around there.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:00.900
Don't think you can run from my Magic Mirror.

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:05.840
I'll send plenty of reinforcements 
and equip them with silver bullets.

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:09.320
It's just the wolfman and the jiangshi?

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:11.410
Where are the others?

00:14:13.860 --> 00:14:15.380
By the way, Wayne,

00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:18.790
how did you gain access to Midnight 
Sun's confidential information?

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:23.210
<i>Maybe I'm a surprisingly sore loser.</i>

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:24.990
Really?

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:28.350
I'm not sure what you did, but keep it up.

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:34.120
Where are the others?

00:14:35.010 --> 00:14:37.200
Were they bait?

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:39.100
Did they trick me?

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:41.110
Don't leave your positions.

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:43.820
I'll find the correct location imme—

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:46.990
What? My surveillance system is down?

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:47.930
Why?

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:52.450
You shut off their surveillance? Really?

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:55.730
So we don't need to play the bait anymore?

00:14:55.730 --> 00:14:57.370
<i>Nope. Good work.</i>

00:14:57.600 --> 00:14:59.370
Make your way from there.

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:00.710
<i>Let's hurry.</i>

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:05.590
<i>I just bought us some time until 
he can get his system back online.</i>

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:09.000
This line...

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:11.930
What is this? I don't recognize this code.

00:15:12.250 --> 00:15:13.800
Who did this?

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:16.400
No signs of unauthorized access.

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:18.180
Admin rights haven't been modified.

00:15:18.710 --> 00:15:20.640
Did I do this?

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:23.400
When did they log in? What day was this?

00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:25.320
<i>I can't escape from the server!</i>

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:29.750
That dual-personality ghost!

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:33.320
He took advantage of the confusion 
to leave some junk in my jail!

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.170
Why do I feel so humiliated?

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:39.540
How could he do this to me?

00:15:40.470 --> 00:15:43.860
You're not a ghost, are you?

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:46.050
You're more interesting than that.

00:15:46.640 --> 00:15:50.090
Just so you know, that demon-like 
side you showed me then...

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:55.040
I've saved it to my memory forever 
so it can never be overwritten!

00:15:57.730 --> 00:16:00.040
They should be around here somewhere.

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:04.530
More monsters from the museum.

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:06.980
Why? Why now?

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:09.380
I'll lure it towards the river.

00:16:09.700 --> 00:16:11.830
Wayne, tell Luke and Toryu.

00:16:11.830 --> 00:16:13.810
Ton, get inside a building.

00:16:13.810 --> 00:16:16.830
No. We don't have time for that.

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:17.860
Hey.

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:19.240
<i>Miss!</i>

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:25.500
<i>Anyway, sorry. I'm bringing 
the system up now,</i>

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:29.000
but I'm going to focus on finding Shinyao.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:32.220
If you want to go after Ton, 
you'll have to find her yourself.

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:35.800
I am. I already found her.

00:16:36.140 --> 00:16:37.790
Oh, really?

00:16:37.790 --> 00:16:39.470
How's she doing?

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:47.980
I can only describe her as unexpected.

00:16:48.390 --> 00:16:52.530
The pawns I have aren't even 
enough to slow her down anymore.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:53.920
Seriously?

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:57.380
I can't let her meet up with Shinyao.
 I need to hurry.

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:00.490
Found you.

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:07.380
What a pleasant breeze.

00:17:12.230 --> 00:17:13.540
What's that?

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:15.040
I'll check it out.

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:16.480
Stay here.

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:17.180
But...

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:20.460
Soon. Soon, he'll...

00:17:20.460 --> 00:17:22.390
Luke and the others will come.

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:23.280
Huh?

00:17:23.280 --> 00:17:25.690
Just wait here a little longer.

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:28.360
It's okay. Then it'll all be over.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:29.610
What do you mean?

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:30.690
What about you?

00:17:31.120 --> 00:17:32.120
Don't worry about me.

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:35.710
It seems I have a bit left to do.

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:42.370
Don't be so reckless.

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:44.760
I'm okay.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:48.130
What is it?

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:52.340
<i>Sorry. I wish I weren't saying this,</i>

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.810
but something unbelievable 
suddenly showed up.

00:17:56.450 --> 00:17:59.330
Our situation is no laughing matter.

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:03.520
You played your final card not 
against Ton, but against them.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:07.090
Fight the unexpected with the unexpected.

00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:08.900
That's standard tactics.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:13.690
Damn. Your ideas are as dirty as ever.

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:20.700
Toryu's keeping it locked 
down someplace deserted,

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:23.200
but with just us, it's a matter 
of time before it gets away.

00:18:23.630 --> 00:18:26.260
<i>Sorry. Come help us.</i>

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:27.920
Got it.

00:18:28.570 --> 00:18:29.440
I'm going.

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:30.580
I'm going with you.

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:33.480
It's really strong, right?

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:35.740
Luke and Toryu can't handle it.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:37.470
You can't go alone.

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:40.720
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:42.480
<i>We don't have time for that.</i>

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:44.970
<i>If you don't hurry, they'll catch Shinyao.</i>

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:47.890
Later.

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:51.830
I'll draw the enemy to me until 
Luke and the others arrive.

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:58.570
You've made things rather difficult.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.560
Are you sure?

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:03.830
I'm not happy about it.

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:08.090
I'm sure Shinyao would tell me to do it.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:12.790
"Don't worry about me. Save your 
friends and the townspeople."

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:17.090
She'd say I wouldn't be me unless I did it.

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:19.480
Hey!

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:30.040
This is...

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:33.480
The reports were accurate.

00:19:33.480 --> 00:19:38.390
It's an extract of the wolfsbane that was 
also effective against your brother.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:40.070
Go to sleep.

00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:42.500
Don't be ridiculous.

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:44.990
I'll protect her.

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:53.410
That's enough.

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:56.760
I had a lot of fun escaping with you.

00:19:58.110 --> 00:19:59.140
Thank you.

00:20:15.930 --> 00:20:17.480
Let's go.

00:20:19.180 --> 00:20:20.650
Don't!

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:26.410
Chris!

00:20:34.350 --> 00:20:35.420
Chris!

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:37.570
No! Chris!

00:20:39.730 --> 00:20:40.760
Take her.

00:20:44.120 --> 00:20:45.410
Target acquired.

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:47.210
Mission accomplished.

00:22:25.270 --> 00:22:27.080
What is this?

00:22:27.650 --> 00:22:28.700
Chris!

00:22:29.350 --> 00:22:32.670
Shinyao, where did you go?

00:22:35.250 --> 00:23:31.760
<b>Phantom 
Twilight Plus</b>

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:37.380
Phantom in the Twilight Plus!

00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:42.250
In this episode, we'll cover
the mysterious Umbra.

00:22:42.250 --> 00:22:43.770
Uh, Chris?

00:22:43.770 --> 00:22:46.140
I know this is your first 
appearance on this segment,

00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:48.540
but didn't you just die in the main series?

00:22:48.540 --> 00:22:49.950
Umbra don't die.

00:22:49.950 --> 00:22:52.530
Even if we're temporarily destroyed,
 we eventually return.

00:22:52.530 --> 00:22:54.200
Really?

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:57.180
Yeah. As long as people 
remember us, we always do.

00:22:57.180 --> 00:22:58.750
Great.

00:22:58.750 --> 00:23:02.480
Then you'll return to me someday.

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:03.220
Not quite.

00:23:03.220 --> 00:23:07.000
Umbra do come back to life,
 but there's no guarantee it'll be me.

00:23:07.000 --> 00:23:07.950
What do you mean?

00:23:07.950 --> 00:23:12.440
The creature that returns 
is the legendary wolfman.

00:23:12.440 --> 00:23:14.520
He won't have my face or memories.

00:23:14.520 --> 00:23:16.410
He'll be someone else.

00:23:16.410 --> 00:23:19.580
So I'll never see you again?

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:21.390
Well, I...

00:23:21.670 --> 00:23:23.120
I don't want that!

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:26.960
If... If you die...

00:23:26.960 --> 00:23:28.270
Wait! Calm down!

00:23:28.270 --> 00:23:30.190
I, uh, well...

00:23:30.590 --> 00:23:33.290
I can't spoil anything else!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:50.090
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:37.180
Shinyao has been kidnapped again,

00:23:37.180 --> 00:23:40.760
but her new role is neither 
hostage nor sacrifice.

00:23:40.760 --> 00:23:43.170
Ton nearly falls to despair and hatred.

00:23:43.170 --> 00:23:45.230
In order to return her 
to the path of humanity,

00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:46.940
Vlad makes a certain choice.

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:50.090
<b>Episode 10 The Day Before Everything Ends</b>

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:49.600
Next time: The Day Before Everything Ends.
